<!-- 1. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY -->
<h1>1. Executive Summary</h1>

<p>Dunco HMS is a comprehensive, web-based Hospital Management System designed to centralize and streamline all hospital operations &mdash; from patient registration and clinical care to billing, pharmacy, laboratory, HR, and management reporting.</p>

<div class="highlight">
    <strong>Built for Kenya. Ready for Africa.</strong><br>
    Dunco HMS is purpose-built for the Kenyan healthcare environment with deep integration into M-Pesa, SHA/SHIF, DHA, and AI-powered clinical support.
</div>

<p><strong>Kenya-Specific Integrations:</strong></p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>M-Pesa (Safaricom Daraja API)</strong> &mdash; Accept payments via STK Push. Patients pay consultation fees, pharmacy bills, and lab charges directly from their phone. Real-time callbacks and automatic invoice reconciliation.</li>
    <li><strong>SHA / SHIF (Social Health Authority)</strong> &mdash; Full eligibility verification, member lookup, authorization requests, claims submission, and coverage tracking through the DHA Health Interoperability Gateway.</li>
    <li><strong>DHA (Digital Health Agency)</strong> &mdash; Patient verification against the national Client Registry, facility lookup, provider verification, and clinical document exchange via the Digital Health Superhighway.</li>
    <li><strong>AI-Powered Healthcare</strong> &mdash; Built-in AI assistants (Elliana D Virtual Nurse) for patient queries, appointment suggestions, diagnosis support, and predictive analytics &mdash; available in English and Swahili.</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>Core Capabilities:</strong></p>
<ul>
    <li>Centralized patient management across OPD, IPD, and emergency</li>
    <li>Integrated billing with M-Pesa, insurance, cash, and card support</li>
    <li>Pharmacy and inventory control with expiry tracking and stock management</li>
    <li>Laboratory and radiology with test requests, results, and PDF reports</li>
    <li>Human resources management including payroll, attendance, leave, and appraisals</li>
    <li>Insurance and claims management with SHA integration</li>
    <li>Telemedicine via Zoom integration</li>
    <li>Patient self-service portal for appointments, results, and billing</li>
    <li>Marketing suite with social media, SEO, AI content writer, and campaigns</li>
    <li>Comprehensive reporting with custom report builder and BI dashboard</li>
</ul>

<div class="highlight">
    <strong>All packages include FREE domain registration (.or.ke or .co.ke) for Year 1 and UNLIMITED professional email accounts</strong> (e.g., info@hospital.or.ke, doctor@hospital.or.ke, pharmacy@hospital.or.ke) &mdash; no per-user charges, no hidden email costs.
</div>

<div class="page-break"></div>

<!-- 2. ABOUT DUNCO HMS -->
<h1>2. About Dunco HMS</h1>

<p>Dunco HMS is developed by <strong>Dunco Web Solutions</strong>, a Kenyan software company specializing in healthcare technology. The system is purpose-built for the Kenyan market with deep integration into local payment systems, insurance frameworks, and health data infrastructure.</p>

<h3>Technology</h3>
<table>
    <tr><th>Component</th><th>Technology</th></tr>
    <tr><td>Backend</td><td>Laravel 12 (PHP 8.2+)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Frontend</td><td>Blade, Alpine.js, Tailwind CSS</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Database</td><td>MySQL 8.0+ with Redis</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Authentication</td><td>Laravel Breeze + Sanctum</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Authorization</td><td>Spatie Permission (21 roles, 95+ permissions)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>PDF</td><td>DomPDF</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Excel</td><td>Maatwebsite Excel</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Backups</td><td>Spatie Laravel Backup</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>Scale</h3>
<table>
    <tr><th>Metric</th><th>Count</th></tr>
    <tr><td>Controllers</td><td>153</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Models</td><td>131</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Blade Views</td><td>457</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Database Migrations</td><td>163</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Configurable Modules</td><td>75+</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Granular Permissions</td><td>95+</td></tr>
    <tr><td>User Roles</td><td>21</td></tr>
</table>

